\subsection{Hard-iron correction result}
\label{sec:mag-hi-results}

The hard-iron correction of Sec.~\ref{sec:mag-hard-iron} is evaluated under the
deterministic protocol rather than the ten-seed OU-family comparison: one
realization per stationary record, default sensor-error draw, and the final
\SI{900}{s}.  With the correction enabled, yaw RMS improves on every one of the
eight records.  The eight-record mean falls from
\SI{1.835}{\degree} to \SI{0.822}{\degree}, and the worst record falls from
\SI{2.162}{\degree} to \SI{1.063}{\degree}.  Pitch improves slightly, while
roll and displacement change negligibly.  The matched OU--II baseline carries
the same magnetic correction, so this improvement does not contribute to the
reported OU--III-minus-OU--II translational difference.

\begin{table}[t]
  \centering
  \caption{Yaw RMS with the continuous hard-iron correction disabled and
           enabled (deterministic protocol, final \SI{900}{s}).}
  \label{tab:mag-hi-yaw}
  \setlength{\tabcolsep}{4pt}
  \renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.08}
  \footnotesize
  \sisetup{detect-all}
  \begin{tabular}{@{}l
                  S[table-format=1.2]
                  S[table-format=1.3]
                  S[table-format=1.3]
                  S[table-format=1.3]
                  S[table-format=1.3]
                  @{}}
    \toprule
    {Case} & {$H_s$} & \multicolumn{2}{c}{Yaw RMS (\si{\degree})}
           & \multicolumn{2}{c}{Pitch RMS (\si{\degree})} \\
    \cmidrule(lr){3-4}\cmidrule(lr){5-6}
    {} & {\si{m}} & {off} & {on} & {off} & {on} \\
    \midrule
    JONSWAP    & 0.27 & 2.075 & 1.063 & 0.174 & 0.175 \\
    JONSWAP    & 1.50 & 1.825 & 1.050 & 0.169 & 0.152 \\
    JONSWAP    & 4.00 & 1.298 & 1.041 & 0.358 & 0.330 \\
    JONSWAP    & 8.50 & 1.104 & 0.709 & 0.469 & 0.445 \\
    \addlinespace
    PM--Stokes & 0.27 & 2.155 & 0.741 & 0.200 & 0.200 \\
    PM--Stokes & 1.50 & 2.162 & 1.026 & 0.223 & 0.208 \\
    PM--Stokes & 4.00 & 2.053 & 0.473 & 0.278 & 0.235 \\
    PM--Stokes & 8.50 & 2.007 & 0.476 & 0.259 & 0.196 \\
    \midrule
    {mean}     & {}   & 1.835 & 0.822 & 0.266 & 0.243 \\
    {worst}    & {}   & 2.162 & 1.063 & 0.469 & 0.445 \\
    \bottomrule
  \end{tabular}
\end{table}

The result is conditional on the shipped calibration draw.  Additional draws
include misalignment-dominated cases in which an additive hard-iron estimator
can regress, because soft-iron and misalignment terms can alias into the fitted
offset while still satisfying the residual gate.  This negative result is the
reason the article does not promote the correction to a complete magnetometer
calibration method; multi-heading excitation is required to identify the larger
distortion model.

\subsection{Embedded portability}
\label{sec:real-hardware-platform}

The same estimator source compiles and executes on an M5Stack AtomS3R
(ESP32--S3) with calibrated MEMS input.  This establishes functional source
portability only.  Processor load, memory use, power, deadline margin, thermal
behavior, and externally referenced wave-reconstruction accuracy were not
measured in the reported study and are not inferred from successful execution.
